Independent Designer: C. Matthew Blackwell
Location: Lafayette, Louisiana
1. Repository Setup & Identity Configuration
To establish secure version control compliance for the SASA-v9.1 core repository, the local environment is configured with cryptographically signed commits matching the independent designer credentials.
# Configure global Git user identity
git config --global user.name "C. Matthew Blackwell"
git config --global user.email "c.matthew.blackwell@independent-architect.sys"

# Initialize local repository for SASA-v9.1
git init sasa-v9.1-core
cd sasa-v9.1-core

# Set up GPG signing key for commit verification
git config --global user.signingkey 0xAE48F91B2C3D4E56
git config --global commit.gpgsign true

2. Branching Strategy & Directory Structure
The repository adheres to a strict multi-tiered branching topology to segregate experimental simulation kernels from production-ready hardware-integrated modules.
 * main: Production-locked branch containing verified simulation releases, cryptographic audit logs, and hardware integration binaries.
 * develop: Integration branch for ongoing multiscale solver updates and AIL supervisor refinements.
 * feature/sasa-c-aggregates: Dedicated branch housing concrete material stress matrices (SASA-C-01 through SASA-C-04) and thermal-structural validation test scripts.
